  "description": "Fuaran.Core.Ops — the skeleton structural ops (InsertChild/RemoveNode/MoveNode/ReorderChildren/Batch/UpdateNode) and the recoverable error-envelope contract (name the failure, enumerate the valid alternatives) — the AI-feedback protocol — plus proposal arbitration (which subset of N op-script proposals can land together against one base tree: batch canApply + greedy footprint independence, a deterministic total partition with typed rejections), the concurrency half of footprint/independent. Per-kind property ops stay domain-side. FSharp.Core only.",
